Language    : Python 3

Description
-----------
This module introduces the basic concepts of input and
output in Python.

Input allows users to provide information while the
program is running. Output displays information from
the program back to the user.

Python provides two built-in functions for this purpose:

1. input()
   Used to receive data entered by the user.

2. print()
   Used to display information on the screen.

Learning Objectives
-------------------
1. Understand the difference between input and output.
2. Learn how to use the input() function.
3. Learn how to use the print() function.
4. Convert user input into different data types.
5. Display formatted output using f-strings.

Functions Used
--------------
input()     Receive data from the keyboard.
print()     Display data on the screen.
int()       Convert string to integer.
float()     Convert string to float.
str()       Convert data to string.

Expected Output
---------------
The program asks the user to enter personal information
and then displays the entered data in a formatted report.

Coding Style
------------
This module follows clean code principles and PEP 8
recommendations for readability, maintainability,
and professional software development.
=========================================================
"""


def main():
    """Main entry point of the program."""

    # =====================================================
    # Receive user input
    # =====================================================

    full_name = input("Enter your full name : ")
    age = int(input("Enter your age       : "))
    height = float(input("Enter your height    : "))
    country = input("Enter your country   : ")

    # =====================================================
    # Display result
    # =====================================================

    print()
    print("=" * 60)
    print("User Information")
    print("=" * 60)

    print(f"Full Name : {full_name}")
    print(f"Age       : {age} years")
    print(f"Height    : {height:.1f} cm")
    print(f"Country   : {country}")

    print("=" * 60)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
